#. Tag: author
#: meridian.docbook:3
#, no-c-format
msgid "<firstname>Jason</firstname> <surname>Harris</surname>"
msgstr "<firstname>Jason</firstname> <surname>Harris</surname>"

#. Tag: title
#: meridian.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Local Meridian"
msgstr "O meridiano local"

#. Tag: primary
#: meridian.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid "Local Meridian"
msgstr "Meridiano local"

#. Tag: indexterm
#: meridian.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid "<seealso>Hour Angle</seealso> <seealso>Celestial Sphere</seealso>"
msgstr "<seealso>Ángulo horario</seealso> <seealso>Esfera celeste</seealso>"

#. Tag: para
#: meridian.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Local Meridian is an imaginary <link linkend=\"ai-greatcircle\">Great "
"Circle</link> on the <link linkend=\"ai-csphere\">Celestial Sphere</link> "
"that is perpendicular to the local <link linkend=\"ai-horizon\">Horizon</"
"link>. It passes through the North point on the Horizon, through the <link "
"linkend=\"ai-cpoles\">Celestial Pole</link>, up to the <link linkend=\"ai-"
"zenith\">Zenith</link>, and through the South point on the Horizon."
msgstr ""
"O meridiano local é un <link linkend=\"ai-greatcircle\">Círculo máximo</"
"link> imaxinario da <link linkend=\"ai-csphere\">esfera celeste</link> que é "
"perpendicular ao <link linkend=\"ai-horizon\">horizonte</link> local. Pasa "
"polo punto norte do horizonte, através do <link linkend=\"ai-cpoles\">polo "
"celeste</link>, do <link linkend=\"ai-zenith\">Cénite</link>, e polo punto "
"sul do horizonte."

#. Tag: para
#: meridian.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Because it is fixed to the local Horizon, stars will appear to drift past "
"the Local Meridian as the Earth spins. You can use an object's <link "
"linkend=\"equatorial\">Right Ascension</link> and the <link linkend=\"ai-"
"sidereal\">Local Sidereal Time</link> to determine when it will cross your "
"Local Meridian (see <link linkend=\"ai-hourangle\">Hour Angle</link>)."
msgstr ""
"Debido a que está fixo no horizonte local, parecerá que as estrelas pasan "
"polo meridiano local a medida que a terra xira. Pode empregar a <link "
"linkend=\"equatorial\">ascensión recta</link> dun obxecto e a <link "
"linkend=\"ai-sidereal\">hora sidérea local</link> para determinar cando "
"cruzará o meridiano local (consulte <link linkend=\"ai-hourangle\">ángulo "
"horario</link>)."
